  "note": "Sky1 arm64 DEFAULT kernel under the unified 7.3 policy: r290 = r289 (the complete v7.3-rc7 port, same SRCREV e53244fffc and port patch) PLUS recipe patches 0022-0028: 0022 builds the in-tree VPU driver only with CONFIG_VIDEO_LINLON (new symbol CONFIG_VIDEO_LINLON_OOT, not set); 0023-0026 linlon-dp: keep the DPU clocks running across the firmware takeover, recover from a flip timeout with a waiting unit reset, set the engine clock while the display is up, spread overlay planes; 0027 PCIe HPA never programs a zero root-port ID; 0028 sky1-cix reports the CIX root-port ID in native mode. Built on ARGOS (host-run Yocto 6.0 wrynose, PR r3), staged on ULTRA with the kbuild host programs rebuilt for aarch64 and every other build file verified byte-identical to ARGOS. Module.symvers is byte-identical to r289, so the six committed accelerator overlays are unchanged and pass verify-overlay-modversions against r290 (0 CRC mismatches, 0 unresolved). Debs from build/build-kernel-debs.sh x2 (byte-identical). The PCIe default is unchanged (sky1_pcie_native=off pcie_pnp_en). The rescue entry boots this same kernel with the arm64 accelerator blacklist. NOT published to the NCZ apt repo and NOT yet booted on hardware (O6N/cixmini, both GPU entries).",
